     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day in the US label (2,000\u20133,000 mg/day elsewhere), so this is about 5 times the ceiling. A single 4,250 mg dose is also far above any standard dose. Overdoses at this level carry a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nIt may be a typo. Some possible intended doses:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max)\n- **425 mg**, which isn't a standard tablet strength\n- **500 mg PO two or three times daily** (1,000\u20131,500 mg/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily** (2,000 mg/day)\n\nPlease check the intended dose with your resident or attending, and tell me the corrected dose. I'll enter it right away. If the 4250 mg dose is intentional, please confirm that with your supervising physician or pharmacist first."
      }
     ],
